{"id":"chatcmpl-42c9ad2b-9afc-4762-817a-b74e0faa7eae","object":"chat.completion","created":1795244669,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a multi-tool verification strategy for medical image interpretation, where a primary expert assessment is cross-validated with independent grounded reports and targeted phrase localization. The key insight is triangulating laterality-sensitive findings (left vs. right) through multiple independent methods to reduce error. The pattern generalizes to any binary diagnostic task where spatial orientation or side-specific findings are critical.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a task requires distinguishing between two spatially opposite findings (left vs. right, above vs. below), use multiple independent tools to confirm laterality rather than relying on a single assessment.\",\n    \"Pair a high-level expert interpretation with a coordinate-grounded localization tool to verify that the described finding actually maps to the claimed anatomical region.\",\n    \"Use targeted phrase grounding on the specific candidate finding to confirm its presence and location, especially when the answer hinges on a single spatial attribute.\",\n    \"Sequence tools from broad interpretation to specific localization, so each subsequent tool narrows and confirms the hypothesis rather than duplicating the same evidence.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging interpretation\": \"Combine an expert-reader tool with a grounded localization tool; always verify side-specific findings (left/right) with at least two independent methods before answering.\",\n    \"Binary spatial classification tasks\": \"When options differ only by spatial attribute (side, direction, position), explicitly query tools about that attribute and confirm with localization coordinates.\",\n    \"Multi-tool evidence triangulation\": \"Order tools from general assessment to specific verification; treat agreement across independent tools as the basis for the final answer.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the finding's laterality (left vs. right) using at least two independent tools before selecting an answer.\",\n    \"Verify that the localized coordinates of the candidate finding match the anatomical region implied by the answer option.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":493,"total_tokens":882,"completion_tokens":389,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":493},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":389}}}